    },
    {
      "claim": "Different folding styles affect how we view the statue (e.g., creating transparency vs. bluntness).",
      "stance": "supports",
      "observation_ids": ["img-k7-o0", "img-v9-o1"],
      "grounds": "The observations confirm that different carving techniques create distinct visual effects. Observation img-k7-o0 states the drapery mimics 'soft, pliable cloth... giving the stone a liquid appearance,' while observation img-v9-o1 notes that specific folding lines and light reflection in another figure create an impression of 'translucency or thinness' and a 'lightweight' look. This supports the hypothesis that the style of the fold alters perception (liquid/soft vs. transparent/lightweight)."
    }
  ]
